I wouldn't look for logic in Nethack food.  Does it make any sense
that meat from a creature just killed could be rotten?  Does it make
any sense that meat from a creature just killed could simply disappear
(ie doesn't leave a corpse)?  Does it make any sense that you can't
smell or otherwise detect rotten food until after you have eaten a
sufficient amount to make you faint?  Can you tell if a banana is
rotten before you eat it?  IIRC, only if you read a blessed scroll of
food detection, will you be able to detect rotten food (or maybe only
tainted food).  Does it make sense that some characters start out with
NO food at all?  And who cooked all those pancakes lying around?  Food
rations in theory should be made with preservatives so they don't
spoil for a long time.  Having said that, perhaps the food ration you
refer to is only partially rotten.

